A remove-only call (no key=value pairs, no appends) drops just the named key; the
rest of the frontmatter and the body stay byte-for-byte intact, and the summary
renders the removal as -<key>.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Probe plan
business_goal: Users find widgets faster.
status: backlog
---

Body.
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md --remove business_goal
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,6 +1,5 @@
 ---
 title: Probe plan
-business_goal: Users find widgets faster.
 status: backlog
 ---
 
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: -business_goal
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Probe plan
status: backlog
---

Body.
-- exit --
0
